Reading this table: 'Logistic Regression' predicts a mean risk of ~0.152
against an observed 0.152 — it is calibrated in the large. The balanced
variant predicts ~0.44 for the same people: identical ranking (see the
spearman column), probabilities inflated ~3x. The extra positives it
catches at the 0.5 cut-off come from that inflation, not from better
discrimination — and the same effect is available for free by lowering
the threshold on the calibrated model (scripts/05).

